  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A solid circular disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> rolls along a horizontal floor so that its center of mass has a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The absolute value of work done on the disc to stop it is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using work-energy theorem, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∆</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>Absolute work <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, required value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
  }
}